--- !u!114 &2142828279
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2142828270}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 310abf78a239ef44b9edb9c10961fbaf, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  bookTitle: Old Book
  readRange: 2
  readKey: 101
  nextPageKey: 101
  prevPageKey: 113
  pages:
  - 'I''ve been stationed here for 30 years.

    The villagers always warned me
    about the forest.



    They spoke of creatures from old stories.

'
  - 'WHITE LADY

    The most feared spirit in these parts.

    A woman in white
    who appears at night.

    Some say she died tragically,

    others say she
    guards the forest.

    She is seen walking alone,

    often near bridges and
    crossroads.



    If you see her...

    Do not look back.

    Do not call
    her name.

    She feeds on fear.

'
  - 'TIKBALANG

    A creature with the head of a horse

    and the body of a man.

    It
    stands taller than any man.

    Its legs are long and powerful.



    It is
    said to be a guardian

    of the mountains and forests.

    It protects nature

    but
    will punish those who harm it.'
  - "I used to laugh at these stories.\r\nNow... I'm not so sure.\r\n\r\nI hear things
    in the forest at night.\r\nFootsteps that don't belong.\r\nFigures in the dark.\r\n\r\nIf
    you're reading this,\r\nI'm probably not coming back.\r\n\r\n\u2014 Guard Captain
    R. Santos\r\n1873"
  pageTitles:
  - OLD GUARD'S JOURNAL
  - page 2
  - page 3
  - page 4
  pageFlipSound: {fileID: 0}
  openBookSound: {fileID: 0}
  closeBookSound: {fileID: 0}
  soundVolume: 0.7
  playerTag: Player
